      "Language": "chi",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": [
        {
          "NlmCategory": "OBJECTIVE",
          "Label": "OBJECTIVE",
          "content": "This study inquired into the relationship between a pentanucleotide repeats(PNR) polymorphism of the apolipoprotein(a)[apo(a)] gene and coronary atherosclerotic heart disease(CHD) in Chinese Han nationality."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "METHODS",
          "Label": "METHODS",
          "content": "PNR polymorphism of the apo(a) gene from 165 cases of CHD and 153 normal individuals were analyzed by polymerase chain reaction(PCR)-denature polyacrylamide gel electrophoresis-silver stain."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "RESULTS",
          "Label": "RESULTS",
          "content": "The frequencies of (TTTTA)(5/8) genotype (0.188) and (TTTTA)(5) allele (0.115) in CHD group were remarkably higher than those in control group (0.039, 0.026)(P<0.01, P<0.05)."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "CONCLUSIONS",
          "Label": "CONCLUSION",
          "content": "These findings indicate that the PNR polymorphism of apo(a) is associated with the susceptibility to CHD, which may be involved in the development of CHD."
        }
      ]},
